# Vanity URLs for printed material and campaigns.
#
# Read from the publish directory by both Cloudflare and Netlify.
#
# Each lands on /instant (the Instant Booking page, since 2026-11-07; it used
# to be the index page) carrying a src tag, so the attribution comes from the
# ONE normal first-touch path — there is no
# second mechanism that could disagree with the sheet. The prefix is what
# selects the segment, per SRC_SEGMENTS in script.js:
#
#   deed- -> movein      dh- -> pro       (no tag) -> direct
#
# 302, not 301: these are marketing URLs and a permanently cached redirect is
# painful to undo once browsers have it.
#
# ONE DASHBOARD REDIRECT RULE EXISTS BY DESIGN: www -> apex, 301.
#
# It is hostname-scoped, not path-scoped, so it never competes with this file
# for authority over a path and cannot shadow anything here. It has to live in
# Cloudflare because a request to www.servecleaning.com is answered before this
# file is ever consulted. 301 there is correct and deliberately unlike the 302s
# below: a marketing slug should stay re-pointable, but www will never resolve
# anywhere other than apex.
#
# The standing rule is NOT "never touch the dashboard". It is: nothing routes a
# PATH where these tests cannot see it. That is how /q first shipped untagged.
# Any other rule you find in the console is a bug until proven otherwise.

/movein   /instant?src=deed-movein   302
/clean    /instant?src=dh-clean      302

# One shared BU alumni email link; tags stay out of the email body.
/bu       /instant?src=email-bu-alumni-01&utm_source=bu_alumni&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=bu_alumni_launch    302

# Business cards.
#
# THESE LIVE HERE, NOT IN THE CLOUDFLARE DASHBOARD. A rule created in the
# dashboard is invisible to this repo and to the test below, which is exactly
# how /q first shipped pointing at an untagged URL. A vanity path in this file
# gets checked; one in the dashboard gets checked by whoever remembers.
#
# The -01 is a PRINT RUN version, not decoration. Reprint with a different
# design and it becomes -02: same channel, two slugs, and the sheet reports
# which card stock or layout actually converted. Free to do now, impossible to
# reconstruct later. Segment comes from the prefix only — everything after the
# first `-` is yours to name, so the version costs nothing.
#
#   qr-  -> pro       the founder card, consumer
#   ref- -> direct    a real person sent them, but we do not know why
#
# A card is handed over in person, so the recipient already had the pitch —
# what they need is the form, and /instant is only the form. (They used to land
# on /#quote; that homepage is becoming the marketplace.)
/q        /instant?src=qr-card-founder-01&utm_source=card&utm_medium=print&utm_campaign=founder    302
/friend   /instant?src=ref-card-friend-01&utm_source=card&utm_medium=print&utm_campaign=referral   302

# /book is the opt-in URL named in Twilio's A2P 10DLC campaign registration.
# A reviewer follows it by hand to confirm the consent checkbox is really there
# and really unchecked, so it has to land ON the booking form: /instant, which
# is nothing but the form. Untagged on purpose: this is a compliance URL, not a marketing one, and
# it must not pollute attribution with a src that no campaign ever printed.
/book     /instant            302
